<title>FINLAND: Outokumpu plans to scrap supervisory board.</title>
<headline>Outokumpu plans to scrap supervisory board.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish metals and mining group Outokumpu Oy said on Wednesday its board would propose that the supervisory board function be disbanded.</p>
<p>&quot;The Ministry of Trade and Industry proposes that the supervisory board function be disbanded,&quot; Outokumpu said in a statement, adding that its executive board was preparing the necessary proposals to change the company's bylaws accordingly.</p>
<p>The Finnish state is Outokumpu's biggest owner with 40 percent of shares.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248, news@Reuters.fi</p>
